    "reasoning": [
      "Each of two 44-MOS master/slave DFFs receives constant high D. Common clearb=0 inhibits both set terms and forces both latch q states low; rising clock transfers the master state to the slave.",
      "UP/DOWN NAND followed by three transistor inverters and NOR with external RESET asserts the common clear only after both requests or explicit reset. There is no ideal internal delay/gate.",
      "Real rppd and diode-connected NMOS establish nb; matched NMOS sink and PMOS reference/mirror form source and sink paths. UP inverter drives the PMOS series switch; DOWN directly drives the NMOS series switch.",
      "VCLAMP cp-to-ground current is positive when the pump delivers charge. Independent integrated channel source-minus-sink agrees closely with external clamp charge but is not a full instantaneous terminal-current KCL claim.",
      "Positive REF lead pumps upward. The frozen VCO has negative tuning gain, so these blocks cannot be directly closed with unchanged polarity."
    ]
  },
